{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/773206-rule-twist-touchstone-merit","id":773206,"title":"Rule Twist: Touchstone Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-24T09:45:01-08:00","id":773206,"title":"Rule Twist: Touchstone Merit","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm looking for a slight way to modify the Touchstone rules. Mainly, I'd like to represent a vampire doubling-down on a single Touchstone as they lose humanity, rather than the current get-more representation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I still like that get-more option, and can see the idea that - as you degenerate more and more, it takes more and more distinct human connections to remind you of what you've lost.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">However, I would also like to add the capability to focus on just one or a few meaningful relationships. My thinking right now is to turn the Touchstone merit into a multi-buy one like Retainer, Language, etc. Each instance of the Merit represents a different Touchstone. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The first dot 'slots-in' the Touchstone into the topmost legal/open humanity rating. Additional dots in an instance allow you to lower the Touchstone's slot by one. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Example:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">My Ventrue has his starting Touchstone as his brother. Because of the Aloof Curse, he's slotted into my Humanity 7 rating. After a mishandled feeding and liberal use of Dominate, I've dropped to Humanity 6. My brother is no longer an attached Touchstone. To re-attach a touchstone I can:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Buy humanity back up to 7.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Buy a new Touchstone Merit and slot them into my Humanity 6 (topmost legal).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Add a dot to my existing <i>Touchstone (Brother)</i> merit, and shift its slot from 7 to 6.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> The latter would be accompanied by a scene to represent that transition. Perhaps I admit what happened, perhaps there's a conflict between the two of us, perhaps some ramification to the feeding event plays out in front of him. Just something thematic to represent the change in relationship.<br /> <br /> As my Ventrue goes through unlife losing humanity, I can keep increasing my <i>Touchstone (Brother)</i> merit to keep him attached.<br /> <br /> Curious if anyone sees any problems with this method (or if I'm missing an aspect on how slotting works). I'd note that it also helps me a lot with NPCs, as I'd like some of my lower Humanity NPCs to have an attached Touchstone, but don't want to spend a lot of creative capital making 3 or 4 of them to get there.<br /> <br /> Misc Qualifiers:<ul><li>Will probably represent the free Touchstone each character gets with a merit on the sheet, but with an X for the first dot to signify a pip that isn't protected by Sanctity of Merits. Dots may be added to it as normal, extra dots <i>would </i>be covered.</li> <li>No more than 6 touchstone merits per character.</li> <li>Ventrue cannot slot a Touchstone into Humanity 1 (Aloof Curse).</li> <li>Might consider a dot or two tax for non-human Touchstones. This could both make them more expensive, and limit how low they could be slotted.</li> </ul>Also, a question:<br /> <br /> When a character loses their first free Touchstone - say it dies - how do other games out there handle the mechanics of acquiring a new one via merit? Do they slot the new one into the slot the free one previously held, or do they skip that slot and go to the next one?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T09:55:20-08:00","id":773211,"title":"","content":"I've been running it this way, usually allowing them to switch a key Touchstone to a lower dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T12:18:20-08:00","id":773320,"title":"","content":"I think this is a pretty legit reinterpretation of the Merit. I have a player who's planning to do essentially this for a future game I'm planning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}